# Update the iOS app on the phone

When the user says "update the ios app on my phone" — or asks to install, reinstall, or sideload the iPhone app — run this from the repo root. Do not read the script, the deploy notes, or the Xcode project first.

```bash
BRAIN2_IOS_TEAM_ID=25YWDVDMKT npm run ios:reinstall -- --force
```

Run it unsandboxed (`all`). Wait for the full build (on the order of 10 minutes). Success is the line `[ios-reinstall] … installed`.

The phone must be unlocked and on the same Wi-Fi as this Mac, or plugged in. The command builds the web app, syncs Capacitor, signs a Debug build for team `25YWDVDMKT`, and installs it with `devicectl`. `--force` installs now; the scheduled job would otherwise wait until the last install is 4 days old.

If it fails because no iPhone is reachable, say so and stop.
